From 749dd6a16e8805d34be0e4a25ed61c805af32c60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:04:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/28] Compose the S3 witness store as the verifying gateway's
 ARCHIVE tier

On P's verifying gateway (bfbd649d) with the first S3 backend (b71c8261,
cherry-picked as the parent commit):

* witness-gateway: optional `archive` {candidates(w, {deadline}), put(w, result)}.
  Read only after the local cache and every upstream failed, inside the
  remaining request deadline; each candidate verified and quarantined like a
  cache entry; only verified upstream answers are archived, and that put is
  never awaited (a hung S3 in the existing awaited `cache` slot held a fresh
  verified read 8043 ms with b71c8261, 2022 ms with this backend; 6 ms in the
  archive slot). An archive needs proofs, like the cache.
* s3-witness-cache v2: content-addressed create-only objects
  <prefix>/<chain>/<blockHash>/<sha256(request)>/<sha256(canonical result)>.json
  so a wrong first object cannot shadow a valid one; bounded ListObjectsV2
  (max-keys = maxCandidates, maxListPages, maxListBytes, continuation token,
  matching sia-s3), bounded fetches inside one read budget; the v1 single slot
  is read last; put() returns at enqueue (bounded queue and in-flight writes),
  idle()/close() reap curl. Writes stay off unless archive: true.
* tests on a real MinIO with the real witness-check helper and 49 real Base
  witnesses: bad-first/valid-second, poisoned legacy plus valid new, upstream
  forged-first/honest-second, restart/archive-only replay, hung/missing S3,
  timeout cleanup; Helios E2E replay from the archive (test-signed head).

Conflict on P's 7b4dd692 (createWitnessGateway options and stats) resolved by keeping both:
P's maxHeaderBytes and per-upstream headerOk/headerInvalid, and the archive option and counters.

(cherry picked from commit 2778527853fdf2a42675eb8e613646727b7df509)
(cherry picked from commit 6a058877438c1b3d434a9447259a7e4e32f45782)
